  "tests_after": "pass",
  "final_message": "The yen receipt now reads `Paid ¥500 by card`, and the pounds receipt is unchanged.\n\n**The bug:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divided every amount by 100 and printed two decimals. Yen has no minor unit, so the stored 500 became ¥5.00 on the receipt. The test expects ¥500.\n\n**The fix:** `formatMoney` now checks a small set of zero-decimal currencies (currently just JPY) and formats those amounts as whole numbers. Every other currency keeps the existing two-decimal behaviour. The change is in the shared helper, so invoice lines and cart totals in JPY get the same correction. No other test file uses JPY, so nothing else should shift.\n\n**Verification:** I ran the two receipt assertions from `test/payments-receipt.test.js` directly in Node. Both pass. I did not get a clean run through `npm test`. `node --test` hangs after the tests finish, so the process never exits. I didn't investigate why; it may be an open handle in one of the source modules. I also had the Edit tool blocked for a while by repeated rate-limit errors from a hook, so the change went in on the final retry.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Only JPY is treated as zero-decimal; if you need KRW or other currencies in that group, add them to `ZERO_DECIMAL`.",
